_projects/web-mirrors/

# Whitelist repo: ignore everything, then re-include only the skill library.
# Rationale: ~/.claude also holds the Obsidian vault (projects/), session
# transcripts, staged drafts and credentials — none of that belongs on GitHub.
*
!.gitignore

# --- skill library ---
!skills/
!skills/**
# Parked skills stay in the repo at their new path — moving a skill out of the
# listing must never remove it from the backup that git provides.
!_skills-coldstore/
!_skills-coldstore/**
!skills-extra/
!skills-extra/**
!skills-adal/
!skills-adal/**
!skills-archive/
!skills-archive/**
!Anthropic-Cybersecurity-Skills/
!Anthropic-Cybersecurity-Skills/**
!agent-native/
!agent-native/**
!plugins/
!plugins/**
!agents/
!agents/**
!agents-root/
!agents-root/**
!commands/
!commands/**

# Plugin cache is machine-local, regenerable runtime state — Claude Code
# repopulates it on plugin install. It is not config and does not belong in
# version control: content-hashed dirs churn on every update, and it carried
# PID lockfiles (.in_use/<pid>), temp shards and orphan markers. Must stay
# BELOW the `!plugins/**` force-include above, or that rule wins.
plugins/cache/
plugins/.last_inuse_sweep

# --- router + agent config ---
!SKILL_ROUTER.md
!CLAUDE.md
!AGENTS.md
!skill-routes.json
!skill_inventory.json
!skill_clusters.json
!README.md
!hooks/
!hooks/**
!scripts/
!scripts/**

# --- machine config (system won't run elsewhere without it) ---
!settings.json

# --- never, even inside the includes above ---
# .mcp.json stays out: it carries a live API key in plaintext.
# skill-usage.jsonl stays out: it holds prompt text, same rule as transcripts.
.mcp.json
skill-usage.jsonl
.credentials.json
*.key
*.pem
.env
.env.*
**/__pycache__/
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/.stfolder/
**/*.mp4
**/*.mov
**/*.zip

# excluded: upstream npxskillui ships a hardcoded Google Fonts API key
skills-extra/npxskillui/src/font-resolver.ts

# Syncthing conflict copies — never commit these; resolve them on disk instead.
*.conflict_*
